    "turn_text": "That moment I was in the audience, in the crime, a short distance from Bobby Kennedy. I had heard earlier that Dr. King had been shot. But that's the only thing I heard. I kept on organizing people, bringing people together. And it was Bobby Kennedy who announced to the crowd that Dr. King had been assassinated. And it was such an unbelievable feeling. I cried. and many, many of the individuals in the audience cried.",
