    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Rosa Parks was just a nice, beautiful, sweet woman with a sense of determination. As a matter of fact, I met Rosa Parks almost a year before I met Dr. King. And I had to attend a program near Nashville, Highlander Folk School, and she was there. And it was a place where blacks and whites could come together. The first time sitting down and having a meal with someone white and Rosa Parks emerged as one of the leaders of this group, apparently she had gone there for many, many years to study the way of nonviolence and social action.",
