  {
    "episode_id": 73253,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/3/73253.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 58,
    "turn_text": "I think the presidency of the so-called leadership of Mr. Trump has set us back, has interrupted the floor of history. But in the final analysis, we will make it the more bridges to cross, but we will make it and it will be the young people, the children that will help us get there in spite of all that is going on today. It just, I just believe deeply within it, just a matter of time. The fate and history will come together. And we would get there. We may be set back for a moment or for a year or two years or maybe longer, but there's no turning back.",
